---
description: AWS CDK and cross-stack wiring
globs: packages/infra/**
---

- Follow `docs/adr/0001-cross-stack-references.md`: no CloudFormation exports for Data/Auth resources. DynamoDB uses the `${tablePrefix}-*` ARN pattern; media bucket and secrets use the SSM registry.
- Follow `docs/adr/0002-cost-optimization.md`: keep the single symptom-based `AppErrors` alarm. Do not add per-table DynamoDB alarms.
- Runtime secrets stay in Secrets Manager; CDK creates empty shells and publishes complete ARNs to SSM. Never put plaintext keys in templates or Lambda env.
- GitHub Actions deploy uses OIDC (`OidcStack`). Do not add long-lived AWS access keys to CI.
- `bin/portfolio.ts` may `addDependency` for deploy ordering. That is not a CFN export.
- Follow `docs/adr/0003-candidate-mcp-server.md` and `docs/adr/0005-candidate-mcp-api-keys.md` for `CandidateMcpStack`: hashed API keys (admin-minted Dynamo rows + optional smoke-test SM secret), no Cognito, no OAuth discovery, Function URL stays `NONE` behind CloudFront origin-verify (not OAC), `grantCandidateMcpDataAccess` stays scoped to five content tables plus `GetItem` on `mcp-api-key` — do not widen to the `${tablePrefix}-*` wildcard used elsewhere.
